IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `imm-entry-and-stay`

-- Immigration Act 1959 (Singapore) -- the offences a private individual meets when dealing with someone else's
-- immigration status: harbouring (s 57(1)(d), (7) to (7D)), employing (s 57(1)(e), (1A), (1B), (8) to (10)), work
-- places (s 57A), marriages of convenience (s 57C), and false information in an application (s 57(1)(k), (ka),
-- (1AAA)); composition (s 59).
--
-- SEAT: the individual who lets a room to, employs, occupies a site with, marries or applies for a non-citizen -- the
-- landlord, householder, employer, spouse or applicant who may be charged.
--
-- Edition: Immigration Act 1959, 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation in force from 30 September 2026, as
-- deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/IA1959.txt.
--
-- NOT ENCODED: s 57(1)(a) to (c), (f) to (j), (l) to (n) (attempts, abetment, conveying, obstruction, using or
-- trading documents, forgery instruments); s 57(2), (2A) (bodies corporate); s 57(11), (12) (letting premises for
-- unlawful employment); s 57B; s 57D (uniforms). The work-place measures prescribed under s 57A(5) were not retrieved.
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written with the writing-l4-rules skill from the individual's seat with the design defaults ruled
-- on 2026-10-18. No pipeline, no coverage table, no independent test pass, no human gate. Not for public use as advice.
-- See NOTES.md.

§ `Immigration Act 1959 -- offences in dealing with a foreigner`

-- Immigration offender (s 57(13)): "a person who has acted in contravention of section 6(1), 15 or 36(1) or the
-- regulations" -- an unlawful entrant, an overstayer, or a removed person who came back. Asked as a fact about the
-- other person; the encoding cannot see their papers.

§§ `57(1)(d), (7) to (7D) -- harbouring`

-- s 57(1)(d): a person who "harbours a person -- (i) whom the defendant knows has acted in contravention ...; (ii) with
-- reckless disregard as to whether he or she has acted in contravention ...; or (iii) negligently failing to ascertain
-- as to whether he or she has acted in contravention".
-- (1AA)(e): (i) and (ii) -- "imprisonment for a presumptive minimum term of not less than 6 months and not more than
-- 2 years and shall also be liable to a fine not exceeding $6,000". (f): (iii) -- "a fine not exceeding $6,000 or ...
-- imprisonment for a term not exceeding 12 months or ... both".
-- (7): proof that the defendant "has given shelter to an immigration offender" raises the presumption of recklessness
-- or negligence "until the contrary is proved".
-- (7A): it is no defence that the person held a permit or pass "unless the defendant further proves that he or she had
-- exercised due diligence to ascertain that the permit or pass was at the material time valid".
-- (7C): due diligence means, against (ii), "any 2 of the acts specified in subsection (7D)"; against (iii), "all the
-- acts". (7D): (a) "inspecting the permit or pass"; (b) "checking the permit or pass to ascertain that the particulars
-- on the passport ... materially correspond"; (c) checking validity with the Controller of Immigration or the
-- Controller of Work Passes, or, where the pass names an employer, with the employer.
-- (7B): a defendant who rebuts the recklessness presumption "shall be liable to be charged" under (iii).
DECLARE `My checks on the lodger` HAS
    `I inspected the permit or pass` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I checked the passport particulars match the permit or pass` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I checked validity with the Controller or with the named employer` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `my checks` IS A `My checks on the lodger`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the number of checks I did` MEANS
         (IF `my checks`'s `I inspected the permit or pass` THEN 1 ELSE 0)
    PLUS (IF `my checks`'s `I checked the passport particulars match the permit or pass` THEN 1 ELSE 0)
    PLUS (IF `my checks`'s `I checked validity with the Controller or with the named employer` THEN 1 ELSE 0)

GIVEN `my checks` IS A `My checks on the lodger`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I rely on the lodger's pass against a charge of reckless harbouring` IF
    `the number of checks I did` `my checks` AT LEAST 2

GIVEN `my checks` IS A `My checks on the lodger`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I rely on the lodger's pass against a charge of negligent harbouring` IF
    `the number of checks I did` `my checks` EQUALS 3

DECLARE `Harbouring charge` IS ONE OF
    `knowing, s 57(1)(d)(i)`
    `reckless, s 57(1)(d)(ii)`
    `negligent, s 57(1)(d)(iii)`

GIVEN `the charge` IS A `Harbouring charge`
GIVETH A Sentence
`What can I be sentenced to for harbouring` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the charge`
    WHEN `negligent, s 57(1)(d)(iii)` THEN Sentence OF FALSE, 0, 12, 6000, FALSE, 0, 0
    OTHERWISE                              Sentence OF TRUE,  6, 24, 6000, FALSE, 0, 0

§§ `57(1)(e), (1A), (1B), (8) to (10) -- employing`

-- s 57(1)(e): a person who "employs any person who has acted in contravention of section 6(1), 15 or 36(1) or the
-- regulations". (1AA)(c): "subject to subsection (1A)", "imprisonment for a presumptive minimum term of not less than
-- 6 months and not more than 2 years and shall also be liable to a fine not exceeding $6,000".
-- (1A): "has at the same time employed more than 5 immigration offenders, the defendant shall be punished with caning
-- in addition" (no number of strokes is stated). (1B): a defendant not punishable with caning shall, "in lieu of
-- caning, be punished with a fine not exceeding $10,000".
-- (8): where an immigration offender "is found at any premises or place, other than premises used solely for
-- residential purposes, the occupier ... is presumed, until the contrary is proved, to have employed him or her knowing
-- that he or she is an immigration offender".
-- (9), (10): a pass is no defence unless the defendant "(a) has inspected the permit or pass"; "(b) has checked" the
-- passport particulars against it; "and (c) where the person employed ... is a holder of a visit pass, has reasonable
-- grounds for believing that the person had, at the material time, in force a work pass ... or had obtained the
-- written consent of the Controller of Immigration".
DECLARE `My hiring` HAS
    `I inspected the worker's permit or pass` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I checked the passport particulars match it` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the worker held a visit pass` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I had reasonable grounds to believe a work pass or written consent was in force` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `my hiring` IS A `My hiring`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I rely on the worker's pass against a charge of employing an immigration offender` IF
        `my hiring`'s `I inspected the worker's permit or pass`
    AND `my hiring`'s `I checked the passport particulars match it`
    AND (   NOT `my hiring`'s `the worker held a visit pass`
         OR `my hiring`'s `I had reasonable grounds to believe a work pass or written consent was in force`)

GIVEN `immigration offenders I employed at the same time` IS A NUMBER
      `I am punishable with caning` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A Sentence
`What can I be sentenced to for employing immigration offenders` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `immigration offenders I employed at the same time` AT MOST 5 THEN Sentence OF TRUE, 6, 24, 6000, FALSE, 0, 0
        IF `I am punishable with caning`                                 THEN Sentence OF TRUE, 6, 24, 6000, TRUE,  0, 0
        OTHERWISE                                                             Sentence OF TRUE, 6, 24, 6000, FALSE, 0, 10000

GIVEN `I occupy the premises where the offender was found` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the premises are used solely for residential purposes` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I presumed to have knowingly employed the offender found there` IF
    `I occupy the premises where the offender was found` AND NOT `the premises are used solely for residential purposes`

§§ `57A -- work places`

-- s 57A(1): "An occupier of a work place who has control of access to the work place must not permit any immigration
-- offender to enter or remain at the work place." (2): if one is found there, control, permission and knowledge are all
-- presumed. (3), (4): rebutted only by "all reasonable measures ... including all the measures prescribed".
-- (6): "a fine of not less than $15,000 and not more than $30,000 or ... imprisonment for a term not exceeding
-- 12 months or ... both for each immigration offender found at the work place and, in the case of a second or
-- subsequent conviction, to a fine of not less than $30,000 and not more than $60,000 or ... imprisonment for a term
-- not exceeding 2 years or ... both for each immigration offender found".
-- "Work place" is defined by reference to construction works (s 57A(7)); asked as a fact.
GIVEN `immigration offenders found at my work place` IS A NUMBER
      `this is a second or later conviction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is the least fine I face if fined as occupier of the work place` MEANS
    `immigration offenders found at my work place` TIMES (IF `this is a second or later conviction` THEN 30000 ELSE 15000)

GIVEN `immigration offenders found at my work place` IS A NUMBER
      `this is a second or later conviction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is the most I can be fined as occupier of the work place` MEANS
    `immigration offenders found at my work place` TIMES (IF `this is a second or later conviction` THEN 60000 ELSE 30000)

§§ `57C -- marriages of convenience`

-- s 57C(1): a person who enters a marriage "(a) knowing or having reason to believe that the purpose of the marriage is
-- to assist one of the parties to the marriage to obtain an immigration advantage; and (b) where any gratification ...
-- is offered, given or received as an inducement or reward to any party to the marriage for entering into the
-- marriage" -- "a fine not exceeding $10,000 or ... imprisonment for a term not exceeding 10 years or ... both".
-- (2): a person who "arranges or otherwise assists in arranging a marriage between 2 other persons, with the intention
-- of assisting one of the parties ... to obtain an immigration advantage" -- the same penalty, with no gratification
-- element. (3): in or outside Singapore. (4): a defence if the defendant "believed on reasonable grounds ... that the
-- marriage would result in a genuine marital relationship" (a question of fact for the court, (5)).
-- (6): "immigration advantage" means "the grant or extension of the validity of any visa, pass, permit or re-entry
-- permit under this Act or the regulations or any order made under this Act for that party or for a child or parent of
-- that party".
DECLARE `My part in the marriage` IS ONE OF
    `I am a party to the marriage`
    `I arranged or helped arrange it`

DECLARE `My marriage facts` HAS
    `my part` IS A `My part in the marriage`
    `I knew or had reason to believe a purpose was an immigration advantage` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I intended to help a party obtain an immigration advantage` IS A BOOLEAN
    `gratification was offered, given or received for entering the marriage` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I believed on reasonable grounds it would be a genuine marriage` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the facts` IS A `My marriage facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do I commit the marriage of convenience offence` IF
        NOT `the facts`'s `I believed on reasonable grounds it would be a genuine marriage`
    AND CONSIDER `the facts`'s `my part`
        WHEN `I am a party to the marriage`
            THEN     `the facts`'s `I knew or had reason to believe a purpose was an immigration advantage`
                 AND `the facts`'s `gratification was offered, given or received for entering the marriage`
        WHEN `I arranged or helped arrange it`
            THEN `the facts`'s `I intended to help a party obtain an immigration advantage`

DECLARE `What is sought` IS ONE OF
    `a visa`
    `a pass`
    `an entry permit`
    `a re-entry permit`
    `citizenship`
    `a job`

DECLARE `For whom` IS ONE OF
    `a party to the marriage`
    `a child or parent of a party`
    `a sibling of a party`

GIVEN `the thing sought` IS A `What is sought`
      `the person it is for` IS A `For whom`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is what is sought an immigration advantage` IF
        CONSIDER `the thing sought`
        WHEN `citizenship` THEN FALSE
        WHEN `a job` THEN FALSE
        OTHERWISE TRUE
    AND CONSIDER `the person it is for`
        WHEN `a sibling of a party` THEN FALSE
        OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `57(1)(k), (ka), (1AAA) -- false information in an application`

-- (k): obtaining or attempting to obtain a permit, pass, visa or certificate "by giving information ... which the
-- firstmentioned person knows" is false or misleading in a material particular -- (1AA)(ga): "a fine not exceeding
-- $8,000 or ... imprisonment for a term not exceeding 12 months or ... both".
-- (ka): the same "by giving information ... that" is false or misleading -- (1AAA): "a strict liability offence";
-- (1AA)(gb): "a fine not exceeding $4,000".
GIVEN `the information was false or misleading in a material particular` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do I commit an offence by the information in my application` IF
    `the information was false or misleading in a material particular`

GIVEN `I knew it was false or misleading` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A Sentence
`What can I be sentenced to for false information in my application` MEANS
    IF `I knew it was false or misleading`
    THEN Sentence OF FALSE, 0, 12, 8000, FALSE, 0, 0
    ELSE Sentence OF FALSE, 0, 0,  4000, FALSE, 0, 0

§§ `59 -- composition`

-- s 59(1): the Controller or an authorised officer "may compound such offence ... as may be prescribed as being an
-- offence that may be compounded by collecting from the person reasonably suspected of having committed the offence a
-- sum not exceeding $2,000". Which offences are prescribed is in the regulations and is not encoded.
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is the most I can be asked to pay to compound an offence` MEANS 2000
